                            <comment id="494354" author="pjo" created="Mon, 11 May 2026 02:08:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged for 2.18&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496080" author="cbordage" created="Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:10:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I am working on the fix for netlink and the patch (not pushed yet) works with regular net import.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But, with ip2nets, there is no way to have different CPTs/tunables between two interfaces of the same net. One way would be to handle:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;ip2nets:
  - net-spec: ${NETTYPE}
    interfaces:
        0: ${INTERFACES[0]}
    ip-range:
        0: &quot;*.*.*.*&quot;
    tunables:
        peer_timeout: 182
        peer_credits: 8
        peer_buffer_credits: 0
        credits: 216
    lnd tunables:
        conns_per_peer: 3
        tos: -1
    CPT: &quot;[0]&quot;
  - net-spec: ${NETTYPE}
    interfaces:
        0: ${INTERFACES[1]}
    ip-range:
        0: &quot;*.*.*.*&quot;
    tunables:
        peer_timeout: 101
        peer_credits: 8
        peer_buffer_credits: 0
        credits: 201
    lnd tunables:
        conns_per_peer: 2
        tos: -1
    CPT: &quot;[1]&quot;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Except if someone has a better option, I think I will take this way.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=hornc&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;hornc&quot;&gt;hornc&lt;/a&gt; You put:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;net:
 - net type: &amp;lt;net&amp;gt;[NUM]
   interfaces:
       0: &amp;lt;intf name&amp;gt;[&apos;[&apos;&amp;lt;expr&amp;gt;&apos;]&apos;]
       1: &amp;lt;intf name&amp;gt;[&apos;[&apos;&amp;lt;expr&amp;gt;&apos;]&apos;]
   tunables:
         peer_timeout: &amp;lt;NUM&amp;gt;
         peer_credits: &amp;lt;NUM&amp;gt;
         peer_buffer_credits: &amp;lt;NUM&amp;gt;
         credits: &amp;lt;NUM&amp;gt;
   lnd tunables:
         &amp;lt;lnd_param1&amp;gt;: &amp;lt;val&amp;gt;
         &amp;lt;lnd_param2&amp;gt;: &amp;lt;val&amp;gt;
         &amp;lt;...&amp;gt;
   CPT: &quot;[&amp;lt;expr]&quot;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;in handle_net_config_sequence description.&lt;br/&gt;
Why did you remove &quot;local NI(s):&quot;? Do you want it optional (to be more like ip2nets)?&lt;br/&gt;
YAML format is kind of a mess because of compatibility and updates. I am trying to fix these issues and keep something clean and simple.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496085" author="cbordage" created="Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:20:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It seems that having several net-spec for ip2nets is not a way (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19436&quot; title=&quot;ip2nets yaml parsing doesn&apos;t adhere to documented behavior&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19436&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19436&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;). So, since there is no need for that in &quot;ip2nets&quot; yet, I will keep in only for &quot;net&quot;. We will see when the feature will be needed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="496341" author="gerrit" created="Thu, 18 Jun 2026 07:06:59 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Cyril Bordage &amp;lt;cbordage@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66707&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66707&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
